1
00:00:00,027 --> 00:00:01,487
(Howard(in Stephen Hawking voice):)You're right.

2
00:00:01,654 --> 00:00:03,574
(Mrs Wolowitz(off):)Who am I kidding?

3
00:00:03,739 --> 00:00:06,619
You should've seen me
when I was young, Sheldon.

4
00:00:06,784 --> 00:00:10,834
(Mrs Wolowitz(off):)The fellas used to line up
and bring me boxes of candy.

5
00:00:12,498 --> 00:00:15,248
(Mrs Wolowitz(off):)Why did I eat it all?

6
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:19,710
(Mrs Wolowitz(off):)Would you hold me?

7
00:00:19,881 --> 00:00:23,171
(Sheldon:)Oh. No, you know,
I'm not really the holding kind of...

8
00:00:23,342 --> 00:00:24,632
(Sheldon:)Oh!

9
00:00:28,514 --> 00:00:30,094
(Howard:)Oh, guys, I just remembered.

10
00:00:30,266 --> 00:00:33,356
l got you some Hawking souvenirs.

11
00:00:33,519 --> 00:00:34,599
(Leonard:)What are these?

12
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:36,770
(Howard:)Gears and springs
from his wheelchair.

13
00:00:36,939 --> 00:00:38,019
(Howard:)Pretty cool, huh?

14
00:00:39,817 --> 00:00:41,487
(Raj:)Wow. That's amazing.

15
00:00:41,652 --> 00:00:43,942
(Howard:)Yeah, I made an adjustment
on the motor drive...

16
00:00:44,113 --> 00:00:46,283
(Howard:)...and when I was putting it
back together...

17
00:00:46,449 --> 00:00:49,489
...l could not for the life of me
figure out where they went.

18
00:00:53,122 --> 00:00:54,202
l did it.

19
00:00:54,373 --> 00:00:56,413
(Sheldon:)Had to go to three clothing stores...

20
00:00:56,584 --> 00:01:02,024
(Sheldon:)...but we finally found a dress
that could envelop your mother.

